# Background tabs

Read `docs/POWER_BUDGET.md`; inspect `packages/web/src/shared/lib/visibility.ts` and the affected lifecycle owner.

- Browser timers can be delayed or suspended. Treat elapsed time as elapsed wall-clock time, not a count of timer ticks.
- Reuse existing visibility/resume utilities when they fit. Preserve deliberately slower background polling; do not introduce an unconditional resume/poll loop.
- Workspace realtime lives in `packages/web/src/shared/lib/workspace-realtime/`. Preserve ordered REST catch-up, cursor generation, WebSocket lifecycle, and runtime ownership.
- Coalesce resume/reconnect triggers and prevent parallel duplicate refreshes. Dispose listeners, timers, and in-flight work when the owner changes.
- Report browser/native validation separately from unit tests when changing background behavior.
